USB identity and descriptor strings
-----------------------------------

Firmware built from this repository enumerates with USB vendor ID 0x0FCF and
product ID 0x1009. These identifiers are present for host driver-matching
compatibility and for no other reason: on Windows the libusb-win32 driver
binds by VID/PID, and every existing host application - Zwift, openant, the
Garmin utilities - locates an ANT USB stick by scanning for exactly those
identifiers. A device that declined to present them would not be found by any
of them, and would not function as the thing it is compatible with.

The descriptor *strings* are the project's own - manufacturer "RadiANT
Project", product "RadiANT ANT+ compatible USB stick". Earlier builds reported
Dynastream's strings; nothing on any host matches on them, so presenting them
was never a compatibility measure and they were changed on 2026-08-11. Where a
host still displays a Dynastream name for this device, it is reading Garmin's
own driver package rather than anything this firmware asserts.

Presenting the numeric identifiers is a compatibility measure, not a claim of
origin, and it is recorded as an open risk rather than a resolved question.
See docs/decisions/0003-naming-trademark-and-usb-identity.md.


Why Apache-2.0
--------------

Apache-2.0 was chosen over MIT or BSD specifically for Section 3, which is an
express grant of patent rights from every contributor with a termination
clause that triggers on patent litigation - a protection that permissive
licences without a patent clause do not provide, and which matters here
because ANT is a patented radio protocol whose patent position has never been
formally cleared. See docs/decisions/0004-license-apache-2-0.md.


Third-party components
----------------------

RadiANT builds against, and optionally links, software owned by others -
including Zephyr and the nRF Connect SDK (Apache-2.0) and, when the sdk-ant
backend is selected, Nordic Semiconductor's proprietary ANT module and the
prebuilt libant.a binary, which carry their own licence terms and a per-unit
royalty. None of that software is redistributed by this repository. The full
inventory, each component's licence, and this project's posture toward it are
in docs/third-party.md.
